.TH DEPLOY-OKD 1 "2026-08-31" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler v1.0.0" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler"
.SH NAME
deploy-okd.sh \- build, push, and deploy the scheduler image to OKD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./scripts/deploy-okd.sh
[\fB\-t\fR \fITAG\fR] [\fB\-r\fR \fIREPO\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fINAMESPACE\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIVALUES\fR]... [\fB\-\-release\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-tls\-secret\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-build\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-cert\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Seven-step deployment: docker build and push, two-pass Helm apply around the
cert-manager TLS secret, deployment restart, rollout wait, status report, and
an HTTPS probe of the route. Requires an active
.BR oc (1)
login. Defaults target the production instance (namespace and release
\fImu2e-shifts\fR, https://mu2e-shifts.fnal.gov) layered with
.IR my-values.yaml .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " TAG"
Image tag (default: exact git tag on HEAD, else \fIlatest\fR).
.TP
.BI \-r " REPO"
Image repository (default docker.io/normanajn/mu2e-shift-scheduler-web).
.TP
.BI \-n " NAMESPACE"
OKD namespace/project (default mu2e-shifts).
.TP
.BI \-f " VALUES"
Helm values file; repeat to layer, later files win (default my-values.yaml).
.TP
.BI \-\-release " NAME"
Helm release name (default mu2e-shifts).
.TP
.BI \-\-tls\-secret " NAME"
cert-manager TLS secret name (default mu2e-shifts-tls).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SEC"
Rollout timeout in seconds (default 180).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-build
Skip the Docker build and push step.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cert
Skip cert-manager; use the router's default wildcard certificate.
.SH EXAMPLES
Production:
.nf
    ./scripts/deploy-okd.sh
.fi
Test instance (https://mu2e-okd-test.fnal.gov):
.nf
    ./scripts/deploy-okd.sh -n mu2e-test --release mu2e-test -t test \\
        --tls-secret mu2e-test-tls \\
        -f helm/simple/values-test.yaml -f my-values-test.yaml
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR build-docker (1),
.BR run-docker-local (1)
